From: kyan0s-git <91159868+kyan0s-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:26:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Rewrite the GLSL shaders for OpenGL 4.1 so they compile
 on macOS

The bundled shaders are GLSL 4.20 and set their binding points with
layout(binding = N), which needs OpenGL 4.2; macOS only provides a 4.1
core profile, so the vertex shader failed to compile and the app crashed
on its first frame. When a shader is loaded, its source is rewritten to
GLSL 4.10 with those qualifiers removed, and after the program is linked
the bindings are set with glUniformBlockBinding and glUniform1i. Uniform
blocks are declared std140, the layout the C++ structs already match.

The SDL context now asks for a forward-compatible core profile on macOS,
falls back to 4.1 when the requested version isn't available, and
reports SDL's error if no context can be created.

From kyan0s-git/engine-sim 56fa977a ("Port to Linux and macOS: vendor
trimmed dependencies, SDL2/OpenGL backend"), adapted to this delta-studio.
